i want fof a to d 4000 streams

You want A0001 → A1000, B0001 → B1000, C0001 → C1000, D0001 → D1000
Total = 4000 streams.

Here is the Bash script to generate the .m3u playlist.

Script for 4000 Streams (A–D)
echo "#EXTM3U" > full_playlist.m3u

for prefix in A B C D; do
  for i in $(seq -w 1 1000); do
    id=$(printf "%s%04d" $prefix $i)
    echo "#EXTINF:-1,Channel $id" >> full_playlist.m3u
    echo "http://iptvcasomsapi.jprdigital.in/x-media/$id/master.m3u8" >> full_playlist.m3u
  done
done
This will generate entries like:

#EXTINF:-1,Channel A0001
http://iptvcasomsapi.jprdigital.in/x-media/A0001/master.m3u8
#EXTINF:-1,Channel A0002
http://iptvcasomsapi.jprdigital.in/x-media/A0002/master.m3u8
...
#EXTINF:-1,Channel D1000
http://iptvcasomsapi.jprdigital.in/x-media/D1000/master.m3u8
The file created:

full_playlist.m3u
Run it Online
You can execute this Bash script on:

Replit → https://replit.com

OnlineGDB → https://onlinegdb.com/online_bash_shell

JDoodle → https://jdoodle.com/bash-shell

Just paste the script and run.

💡 If you want, I can also give you a much more powerful script that scans which of the 4000 streams actually work and creates a clean .m3u automatically (very useful for IPTV).


